@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - **Fair bonus trade pricing (building-effect aware).** In `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, add a quick pre-check that scales a bonus’s trade value by how many **citywide building effects it actually unlocks with current techs** (granary/market/grocer/harbor/temple/monastery, etc.). Wonders/cathedrals ignored; less pronounced for coastal-building effects, as we assume to simplify many cities aren’t coastal and thus wouldn’t benefit. **Practical result (examples):** Maize/Wheat/Grapes are priced noticeably higher than Pigs/Cows; Molluscs beat low-impact foods; Iron is valued slightly less than before when it has no building bonuses (should still be valuable for units). **Effect:** shuts down early GPT farming, makes AI↔AI swaps fairer, and strengthens AI openings/midgame. See **[KI#66](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#66---fixed-and-greatly-enhanced-ai-overvaluing-bonuses-that-give-minor-effects-such-as-pig-or-cattlecow-1-health-only-etc-that-ai-would-value-the-same-as-maize-or-wheat-2-health-effectively-since-almost-all-cities-have-a-granary-and-very-early-anyways-etc-or-grapes-from-grocer-or-molluscs-from-harbor-for-example-by-adding-a-pre-check-in-cvplayeraiai_bonustradeval-to-value-relatively-more-bonuses-the-more-effects-they-provide-from-buildings-if-we-have-their-required-tech-of-these-buildings-so-that-humans-cant-abuseexploit-it-with-aggressive-trading-to-become-super-rich-xd-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-and-also-in-ai-vs-ai-trading-each-ai-gets-best-or-more-value-out-of-the-effective-value-of-their-bonuses-at-least-more-so-now-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc)**.
 - **Bonus trade valuation uses `iAIObjective`:** In `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, the AI now factors each bonus’s `iAIObjective` weight directly into price—higher-priority strategic bonuses (per your weights) command more value in trades.
 - **Era- & inventory-aware relative pricing for key strategic bonuses (Horse↔Camel, Camel↔Horse, ±Elephants):** Also in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, trade values now adjust by what the buyer already has and by era. Examples: Medieval buyer with **Horse/Camel** but no **Iron** values Iron ≈ x2 (to unlock Knights); by Renaissance that premium fades (Muskets don’t need any bonus; Cannons only need Iron). **Elephants** are valued in Ancient/Classical, but discounted in Medieval (≈ x0.5, for buildings at most). **Copper/Iron** are discounted in Classical if the buyer already has Camel/Horse/Elephants; Horse and Camel are treated as partial substitutes early on. **Update:** this adjustment no longer applies to trades *within* the same master–vassal(s) locus, since it is generally in their shared interest to strengthen each other.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5161+) **Aggressive tech trade discounts for widely known techs:** AIs now sell technologies known by ≥1 of their rivals at **heavy discounts** (e.g. 25% of the original cost/value), recognizing that it is better to secure **some gold** immediately via a cheap sale than to hold out and risk getting **0 gold** if a rival sells it first; implemented in `CvPlayerAI::AI_dealVal`. To compensate for this higher trading efficiency, **AI research costs** (`iAIResearchPercent`) have been adjusted (reduced/increased at higher/lower difficulties). See [KI#83](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#83---tremendously-improved-ais-not-trading-techs-more-aggressively-and-cheaply-when-rivals-discover-them-too-and-there-is-a-risk-they-will-beat-us-to-the-sale-leaving-us-with-nothing-rather-than-little-gold-or-such-which-would-have-been-much-better).
 - **Preferential master–vassal tech trading:** Heavily increase willingness to trade techs with our **master/vassal(s)**; change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises with the earlier “devalue techs your master/vassal already knows” change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and extends it **to *all* techs**, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to **reduce tech overlap** and **improve sharing** between vassals (who had many more techs) and their master (who now picks up more of them). Also updated `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` to pass an explicit probability multiplier (rather than relying on the default of 1), making tech-trade frequency more dynamic and tunable instead of solely personality-driven. See [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--add-a-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-to-have-a-more-dynamic-tech-trading-not-only-based-on-personality-according-to-chatgpt-51-and-then-corrected-by-claude-sonnet-45s-review-check-if-accurate-anyways-etc). **Update:** Extend the same extra trade bias to **sibling vassal↔vassal** trades.
 - **Military-power–aware tech trade targeting:** If a potential tech-trade is *not* between members of the same master–vassal(s) locus, `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo` instead increases tech-trade contact chance toward **militarily weaker** players (safer, less likely to threaten us) and reduces it for **stronger** ones (less free value to future rivals). In one autoplay sample this seemingly produced a much closer game: the former runaway (Ewuare) was repeatedly caught up by rivals, and the game lasted to ~T419 instead of ~T288, with the lead changing hands several times. See [KI#80](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#80---tremendously-improved-ai-contacting-for-tech-trades-players-that-are-stronger-even-though-this-is-more-likely-to-be-detrimental).
 - **Master–vassal(s) locus first for tech trades:** Whenever the AI wants to contact other players for a tech trade in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`, it now **first checks** whether the desired tech is already tradeable inside its own master–vassal locus (master, vassals, sibling vassals). If so, it **does not ask outside civilizations for that tech**, nudging trades to stay within the group instead. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to help Ewuare win earlier by finally picking up the Dragoon-related military tech from a vassal, while the locus kept a similar overall tech pace to previous runs. See [KI#79](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#79---improved-before-contacting-other-players-for-tech-trades-first-check-if-we-dont-already-have-the-tech-in-our-master-vassals-locus-and-if-so-dont-contact-the-other-players).

